## 1. Host Discovery

### Ping Scan

Discover live hosts without performing a port scan:

```bash
nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24
```

### Disable Host Discovery

Treat all hosts as online:

```bash
nmap -Pn 192.168.1.10
```

---

## 2. Port Scanning

### Fast Scan

Scan the top 100 ports:

```bash
nmap -F <target>
```

### Scan All Ports

Scan all 65,535 TCP ports:

```bash
nmap -p- <target>
```

### Scan Specific Ports

```bash
nmap -p 22,80,443 <target>
```

### Scan a Port Range

```bash
nmap -p 1-1000 <target>
```

---

## 3. Service & Version Detection

### Service Version Detection

Detect services and their versions:

```bash
nmap -sV <target>
```

### Aggressive Scan

Enable OS detection, version detection, script scanning, and traceroute:

```bash
nmap -A <target>
```
